I just noticed yesterday, in my last pre-Gehennom cleaning up of the
dungeon with my Flame Mage, that what I had thought was one of those
ubiquitous "ghost corpses" (where you leave a room while there's a corpse
visible, and until you re-enter the room it still appears to be there) was
actually a grey elf corpse, undecayed after over 90,000 turns since it was
killed. I haven't had the nerve to pick it up, or try to eat it or tin it,
or even remove any of the armor or weapons from the small pile it's on top
of, since it's wonderfully mystifying, like a flipped coin that lands on
edge. After discovering this, I went away from the level for a subtantial
amount of time (another 700 turns) and it was still there when I returned.
I have to wonder whether this is sort of thing has happened to anyone else
ever before, and if not, how exactly to figure out how such a thing should
be possible.
The level it's on is a little atypical in that it contains the portal to
One-Eyed Sam's Black Market, plus two "swamp" rooms and a weapon shop, but
random monsters still appear, and their corpses vanish normally (a mess of
gibberlings was a good test case), so I doubt it could be some general
property of the level.
What the heck could make an exposed, normal corpse act like it was in an
icebox, if it's not a bug?

